      "nets": ["VOUTN", "VOUTP"],
      "observed": "R36 is assigned the value 24k, but its MPN is FRC0805J240TSD and its description specifies 24Ω.",
      "expected": "The sourced part should be 24k to match the schematic value, or the schematic value and design intent should be corrected if 24Ω is intended.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R36\") (value \"24k\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(field (name \"MPN\") \"FRC0805J240TSD\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(description \" 125mW Thick Film Resistors 150V ±100ppm/℃ ±5% 24Ω 0805 Chip Resistor - Surface Mount ROHS\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"R36\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"R36\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If the listed MPN is used for sourcing, R36 will be about 1000 times lower in resistance than the schematic specifies, heavily loading the VOUTP–VOUTN output and potentially preventing it from operating as intended.",
      "confidence": 0.91
    }
  ],
  "summary": "R36 has a clear value-to-sourcing metadata conflict: the schematic says 24k, while its MPN and description identify a 24Ω part. If the MPN governs assembly, this substantially changes the output loading."
}

